"First, simplify the left side of the equation:\n\n\\[5^b + 5^b + 5^b + 5^b + 5^b = 5 \\cdot 5^b\\]\n\nNext, simplify the right side of the equation:\n\n\\[625^{(b-1)} = (5^4)^{b-1} = 5^{4(b-1)}\\]\n\nNow, set the two expressions equal to each other:\n\n\\[5 \\cdot 5^b = 5^{4(b-1)}\\]\n\nSince the bases are the same, we can equate the exponents:\n\n\\[b = 4(b-1)\\]\n\nSolve for \\(b\\):\n\n\\[b = 4b - 4\\]\n\\[4 = 3b\\]\n\\[b = \\frac{4}{3}\\]\n\nTherefore, the value of \\(b\\) is \\(\\boxed{\\frac{4}{3}}\\)."
"To rewrite the quadratic $4x^2 + 2x - 1$ in the form \\(a(x+b)^2 + c\\), we complete the square.\n\nFirst, factor out the coefficient of \\(x^2\\) from the first two terms:\n\\[4(x^2 + \\frac{1}{2}x) - 1\\]\n\nNext, complete the square inside the parentheses:\n\\[4(x^2 + \\frac{1}{2}x + \\frac{1}{4} - \\frac{1}{4}) - 1\\]\n\\[4((x + \\frac{1}{2})^2 - \\frac{1}{4}) - 1\\]\n\\[4(x + \\frac{1}{2})^2 - 1\\]\n\nThus, \\(a = 4\\), \\(b = \\frac{1}{2}\\), and \\(c = -1\\).\n\nTherefore, \\(a + b + c = 4 + \\frac{1}{2} - 1 = 4 + \\frac{1}{2} = 4.5\\).\n\nFinal Answer: The final answer is $4.5$. I hope it is correct."
