"Let $g$ be the weight of one green ball and $r$ be the weight of one red ball. We have the following system of equations:\n\n\\begin{align*}\n5g + 2r &= 10, \\\\\ng + 4r &= 7.\n\\end{align*}\n\nWe can solve this system by elimination or substitution. Let's use elimination. First, multiply the first equation by 2:\n\n\\begin{align*}\n10g + 4r &= 20.\n\\end{align*}\n\nNow, subtract the second equation from this:\n\n\\begin{align*}\n9g &= 13.\n\\end{align*}\n\nSo, $g = \\frac{13}{9}$. Now, we need to find the weight of $8$ red and $8$ green balls together. This is $8r + 8g = 8(g + r) = 8 \\cdot \\frac{13}{9} = \\boxed{13}$."
