"To determine how much greater \\(43^2\\) is compared to \\(27^2\\), we first need to calculate the values of \\(27^2\\) and \\(43^2\\).\n\n1. Calculate \\(27^2\\):\n\\[\n27^2 = 27 \\times 27 = 729\n\\]\n\n2. Calculate \\(43^2\\):\n\\[\n43^2 = 43 \\times 43 = 1849\n\\]\n\n3. Find the difference between \\(43^2\\) and \\(27^2\\):\n\\[\n43^2 - 27^2 = 1849 - 729 = 1120\n\\]\n\nTherefore, \\(43^2\\) is \\(\\boxed{1120}\\) greater than \\(27^2\\)."
"We can use the identity $x^3 - y^3 = (x - y)(x^2 + xy + y^2)$.\n\nFirst, we need to find the value of $xy$. We can use the equation $(x - y)^2 = x^2 + y^2 - 2xy$.\n\nSubstituting the given values, we have:\n\n$6^2 = 24 - 2xy$\n\n$36 = 24 - 2xy$\n\n$2xy = -12$\n\n$xy = -6$\n\nNow, we can use the identity to find $x^3 - y^3$:\n\n$x^3 - y^3 = (x - y)(x^2 + xy + y^2)$\n\n$x^3 - y^3 = 6(24 - 6)$\n\n$x^3 - y^3 = 6(18)$\n\n$x^3 - y^3 = 108$\n\nTherefore, $x^3 - y^3 = \\boxed{108}$."
