"To find the total number of chimes the clock will strike in a twelve-hour period, we need to sum the number of chimes for each hour from 1 to 12. This is the sum of the first 12 positive integers.\n\nThe formula for the sum of the first \\( n \\) positive integers is:\n\\[\nS = \\frac{n(n + 1)}{2}\n\\]\n\nFor \\( n = 12 \\):\n\\[\nS = \\frac{12 \\times 13}{2} = \\frac{156}{2} = 78\n\\]\n\nTherefore, the total number of chimes the clock will strike in a twelve-hour period is \\(\\boxed{78}\\)."
