"First, we simplify the given equation:\n\n$$\\frac{x^{r-2}\\cdot y^{2s}\\cdot z^{3t+1}}{x^{2r}\\cdot y^{s-4}\\cdot z^{2t-3}} = xyz$$\n\nCombine the exponents in the numerator and the denominator:\n\n$$x^{r-2-2r}\\cdot y^{2s-s-4}\\cdot z^{3t+1-2t-3} = xyz$$\n\nSimplify the exponents:\n\n$$x^{-2}\\cdot y^{s}\\cdot z^{-2} = xyz$$\n\nThis implies that:\n\n$$r = -2$$\n$$s = 1$$\n$$t = -2$$\n\nNow, we need to find $r^s \\cdot t$:\n\n$$r^s \\cdot t = (-2)^1 \\cdot (-2) = -2 \\cdot (-2) = 4$$\n\nTherefore, the answer is:\n\n$$\\boxed{4}$$"
