"To determine how many miles William ran, we need to use the formula for distance, which is:\n\n\\[ \\text{Distance} = \\text{Speed} \\times \\text{Time} \\]\n\nGiven:\n- Speed = 8 miles per hour\n- Time = 75 seconds\n\nFirst, we need to convert the time from seconds to hours because speed is given in miles per hour. There are 3600 seconds in an hour, so:\n\n\\[ \\text{Time in hours} = \\frac{75}{3600} = \\frac{1}{48} \\text{ hours} \\]\n\nNow, we can calculate the distance:\n\n\\[ \\text{Distance} = 8 \\text{ miles per hour} \\times \\frac{1}{48} \\text{ hours} = \\frac{8}{48} = \\frac{1}{6} \\text{ miles} \\]\n\nTherefore, William ran \\(\\boxed{\\frac{1}{6}}\\) miles."
