"To find \\( f(8) \\), we need to substitute \\( x = 8 \\) into the function \\( f(x) = 3\\sqrt{2x - 7} - 8 \\).\n\nFirst, substitute \\( x = 8 \\) into the function:\n\\[ f(8) = 3\\sqrt{2(8) - 7} - 8 \\]\n\nNext, simplify inside the square root:\n\\[ 2(8) - 7 = 16 - 7 = 9 \\]\n\nSo the function becomes:\n\\[ f(8) = 3\\sqrt{9} - 8 \\]\n\nNow, calculate the square root:\n\\[ \\sqrt{9} = 3 \\]\n\nSo the function becomes:\n\\[ f(8) = 3 \\cdot 3 - 8 \\]\n\nFinally, perform the multiplication and subtraction:\n\\[ f(8) = 9 - 8 = 1 \\]\n\nTherefore, the value of \\( f(8) \\) is \\(\\boxed{1}\\)."
