"We have that $T(b+1)-T(b)=\\frac{(b+1)(b+2)}{2}-\\frac{b(b+1)}{2}=\\frac{b+2}{2}$. Therefore, we need to find the smallest integer $b>2011$ such that $\\frac{b+2}{2}=T(x)$ for some positive integer $x$. Since $T(x)=\\frac{x(x+1)}{2}$, we have $\\frac{b+2}{2}=\\frac{x(x+1)}{2}$. Therefore, $b+2=x(x+1)$. We need to find the smallest integer $b>2011$ such that $b+2=x(x+1)$ for some positive integer $x$. We can do this by trying different values of $x$ and solving for $b$. We find that $b=2012$ is the smallest integer that satisfies this condition. Therefore, the smallest integer $b>2011$ such that $T(b+1)-T(b)=T(x)$ for some positive integer $x$ is $\\boxed{2012}$."
"To find the volume of the cone, we use the given formula \\( V = \\frac{1}{3}Bh \\), where \\( B \\) is the area of the base and \\( h \\) is the height of the cone.\n\nGiven:\n- Area of the base \\( B = 30 \\) square units\n- Height \\( h = 6.5 \\) units\n\nSubstitute the given values into the formula:\n\\[ V = \\frac{1}{3} \\times 30 \\times 6.5 \\]\n\nFirst, perform the multiplication:\n\\[ 30 \\times 6.5 = 195 \\]\n\nThen, multiply by \\(\\frac{1}{3}\\):\n\\[ V = \\frac{1}{3} \\times 195 = 65 \\]\n\nTherefore, the volume of the cone is \\(\\boxed{65}\\) cubic units."
