"To find the value of \\( x \\) at the point of intersection of the two lines, we need to solve the system of equations:\n\n1. \\( y = 2x - 13 \\)\n2. \\( 3x + y = 92 \\)\n\nFirst, substitute the expression for \\( y \\) from the first equation into the second equation:\n\n\\[ 3x + (2x - 13) = 92 \\]\n\nSimplify the equation:\n\n\\[ 3x + 2x - 13 = 92 \\]\n\\[ 5x - 13 = 92 \\]\n\nAdd 13 to both sides:\n\n\\[ 5x = 105 \\]\n\nDivide by 5:\n\n\\[ x = 21 \\]\n\nTherefore, the value of \\( x \\) at the point of intersection is \\(\\boxed{21}\\)."
