"To find the length of the line segment with endpoints \\((-3,7)\\) and \\(2,- 5)\\), we use the distance formula:\n\n\\[\nd = \\sqrt{(x_2 - x_1)^2 + (y_2 - y_1)^2}\n\\]\n\nSubstituting the given coordinates:\n\n\\[\nd = \\sqrt{(2 - (-3))^2 + (-5 - 7)^2}\n\\]\n\n\\[\nd = \\sqrt{(2 + 3)^2 + (-5 - 7)^2}\n\\]\n\n\\[\nd = \\sqrt{5^2 + (-12)^2}\n\\]\n\n\\[\nd = \\sqrt{25 + 144}\n\\]\n\n\\[\nd = \\sqrt{169}\n\\]\n\n\\[\nd = 13\n\\]\n\nTherefore, the length of the line segment is \\(\\boxed{13}\\) units."
