"To determine how many factorials from 1! to 100! are divisible by 9, we need to consider the properties of factorials and divisibility by 9.\n\nFirst, note that \\(9 = 3^2\\). For a factorial to be divisible by 9, it must include at least two factors of 3. This means the factorial must include at least \\(3^2 = 9\\).\n\nThe factorial of a number \\(n\\) includes all integers from 1 up to \\(n\\). Therefore, \\(n!\\) will be divisible by 9 if and only if \\(n \\geq 3\\).\n\nThus, the factorials from 1! to 100! that are divisible by 9 are \\(3!\\), \\(4!\\), \\(5!\\), ..., \\(100!\\).\n\nCounting these, we see that there are 98 such factorials.\n\nTherefore, the number of factorials from 1! to 100! that are divisible by 9 is \\(\\boxed{98}\\)."
