"To determine the probability that the sum of two fair 6-sided dice is 9, we need to identify all the possible outcomes that result in a sum of 9 and then divide by the total number of possible outcomes.\n\nFirst, let's list the possible outcomes that result in a sum of 9:\n1. (3, 6)\n2. (4, 5)\n3. (5, 4)\n4. (6, 3)\n\nThere are 4 such outcomes.\n\nNext, we calculate the total number of possible outcomes when rolling two 6-sided dice. Since each die has 6 faces, the total number of outcomes is:\n\n\\[ 6 \\times 6 = 36 \\]\n\nNow, the probability of rolling a sum of 9 is the number of favorable outcomes divided by the total number of possible outcomes:\n\n\\[ \\text{Probability} = \\frac{\\text{Number of favorable outcomes}}{\\text{Total number of possible outcomes}} = \\frac{4}{36} = \\frac{1}{9} \\]\n\nTherefore, the final answer is \\(\\frac{1}{9}\\). I hope it is correct."
"Let the initial value of the stock be \\( V \\).\n\nOn Monday, the stock loses 10% of its value, so the value at the end of Monday is:\n\\[ V - 0.1V = 0.9V. \\]\n\nOn Tuesday, the stock loses 20% of the value it had at the end of Monday, so the value at the end of Tuesday is:\n\\[ 0.9V - 0.2 \\times 0.9V = 0.9V - 0.18V = 0.72V. \\]\n\nThe overall percent loss in value from the beginning of Monday to the end of Tuesday is:\n\\[ V - 0.72V = 0.28V. \\]\n\nThe overall percent loss is:\n\\[ \\left( \\frac{0.28V}{V} \\right) \\times 100\\% = 28\\% \\]\n\nTherefore, the overall percent loss in value from the beginning of Monday to the end of Tuesday is \\(\\boxed{28\\%}\\)."
"Let the width of the original garden be $w$ and the length be $2w$. The perimeter of the original garden is $2(w + 2w) = 6w$. When the perimeter is doubled, the new perimeter is $2 \\times 6w = 12w$. The new shape is a square, so the side length of the square is $6w$. The area of the square is given by $6w^2 = 3600$. Solving for $w$, we get $w^2 = 100$, so $w = 10$. Therefore, the width of the original garden is $10$ feet and the length is $2 \\times 10 = 20$ feet. The area of the original garden is $10 \\times 20 = 200$ square feet.\n\nFinal Answer: The final answer is $200$. I hope it is correct."
