"Let \\( d \\) be the number of dresses produced and \\( s \\) be the number of shirts produced. According to the problem, the ratio of dresses to shirts is 3:5. This can be written as:\n\n\\[\n\\frac{d}{s} = \\frac{3}{5}\n\\]\n\nThe total number of garments produced is 72. Therefore, we can write:\n\n\\[\nd + s = 72\n\\]\n\nSubstituting the ratio into the equation, we get:\n\n\\[\n\\frac{3}{5}s + s = 72\n\\]\n\nCombining the terms, we have:\n\n\\[\n\\frac{8}{5}s = 72\n\\]\n\nSolving for \\( s \\), we get:\n\n\\[\ns = 72 \\times \\frac{5}{8} = 45\n\\]\n\nNow, using the ratio to find \\( d \\):\n\n\\[\nd = \\frac{3}{5}s = \\frac{3}{5} \\times 45 = 27\n\\]\n\nThus, the number of dresses produced is:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{27}\n\\]"
