"In an isosceles right triangle, the legs are congruent, and the hypotenuse is \\(\\sqrt{2}\\) times the length of each leg. Let the length of each leg be \\(x\\). Then the hypotenuse is \\(x\\sqrt{2}\\).\n\nGiven that the hypotenuse is 20 units, we have:\n\\[ x\\sqrt{2} = 20 \\]\n\nSolving for \\(x\\):\n\\[ x = \\frac{20}{\\sqrt{2}} = 10 \\]\n\nThe area of the triangle is given by:\n\\[ \\text{Area} = \\frac{1}{2} \\times \\text{leg}_1 \\times \\text{leg}_2 = \\frac{1}{2} \\times 10 \\times 10 = 50 \\]\n\nTherefore, the area of the isosceles right triangle is \\(\\boxed{50}\\) square units."
