"To determine how long it will take for the lion to catch the elephant, we need to calculate the relative speed between the lion and the elephant. Since they are running towards each other, we add their speeds:\n\n\\[ 24 \\text{ miles per hour} + 19 \\text{ miles per hour} = 43 \\text{ miles per hour} \\]\n\nThe distance between the lion and the elephant is initially 1 mile. To find the time it takes for the lion to catch the elephant, we divide the distance by the relative speed:\n\n\\[ \\frac{1 \\text{ mile}}{43 \\text{ miles per hour}} = \\frac{1}{43} \\text{ hours} \\]\n\nSince there are 60 minutes in an hour, we convert the time to minutes:\n\n\\[ \\frac{1}{43} \\text{ hours} \\times 60 \\text{ minutes per hour} = \\frac{60}{43} \\text{ minutes} \\approx 1.40 \\text{ minutes} \\]\n\nFinal Answer: The final answer is 1.40 minutes. I hope it is correct."
