"To determine how many times all three lights will come on at the same time during a seven-minute dance, we need to find the least common multiple (LCM) of their blinking intervals. The blinking intervals are 2 seconds, 3 seconds, and 5 seconds.\n\nFirst, we find the LCM of 2 and 3:\n\\[\n\\text{LCM}(2, 3) = 6\n\\]\n\nNext, we find the LCM of 6 and 5:\n\\[\n\\text{LCM}(6, 5) = 30\n\\]\n\nThus, the LCM of 2, 3, and 5 is 30 seconds.\n\nNow, we need to determine how many 30-second intervals fit into 7 minutes:\n\\[\n7 \\text{ minutes} = 420 \\text{ seconds}\n\\]\n\\[\n\\frac{420 \\text{ seconds}}{30 \\text{ seconds/interval}} = 14 \\text{ intervals}\n\\]\n\nTherefore, all three lights will come on at the same time \\boxed{14} times during the seven-minute dance."
