"To find the total number of students in the homeroom class, we can use the principle of inclusion and exclusion. Let's denote the number of students taking biology as \\( B \\), the number of students taking Spanish as \\( S \\), and the number of students taking both biology and Spanish as \\( B \\).\n\nGiven:\n- \\( B = 18 \\)\n- \\( S = 13 \\)\n- \\( B = 5 \\)\n\nThe principle of inclusion and exclusion states that the total number of students in the class is the sum of the number of students taking biology and the number of students taking Spanish, minus the number of students taking both subjects:\n\n\\[\n\\text{Total number of students} = B + S - B\n\\]\n\nSubstituting the given values:\n\n\\[\n\\text{Total number of students} = 18 + 13 - 5 = 26\n\\]\n\nTherefore, the total number of students in the homeroom class is \\(\\boxed{26}\\)."
"To find \\(\\frac{x}{y}\\) given \\(x = \\frac{5}{8}\\) and \\(y = \\frac{5}{3}\\), we simply divide \\(x\\) by \\(y\\):\n\n\\[\n\\frac{x}{y} = \\frac{\\frac{x}{y}}{\\}}{\\frac{x}{y}} = \\frac{\\frac{5}{8}}{\\frac{5}{3}} = \\frac{5}{8} \\times \\frac{3}{5} = \\frac{3}{8}\n\\]\n\nTherefore, the value is \\(\\boxed{\\frac{3}{8}}\\)."
"To find the value of \\( x \\) in the given diagram, we need to use the fact that the sum of the angles in a triangle is \\( 180^\\circ \\).\n\nGiven:\n- One angle is \\( 2x^\\circ \\).\n- Another angle is \\( 3x^\\circ \\).\n\nThe sum of the angles in a triangle is:\n\\[ 2x^\\circ + 3x^\\circ = 180^\\circ \\]\n\nCombine like terms:\n\\[ 5x^\\circ = 180^\\circ \\]\n\nSolve for \\( x \\):\n\\[ x = \\frac{180^\\circ}{5} \\]\n\\[ x = 36^\\circ \\]\n\nTherefore, the value of \\( x \\) is \\(\\boxed{36}\\)."
