"To solve the expression \\(\\sqrt{x^2} - 3\\) when \\(x = 6\\), we will follow these steps:\n\n1. Substitute \\(x = 6\\) into the expression.\n2. Simplify the expression inside the square root.\n3. Calculate the square root.\n4. Subtract 3 from the result.\n\nLet's go through each step in detail:\n\n1. Substitute \\(x = 6\\) into the expression:\n   \\[\n   \\sqrt{6^2} - 3\n   \\]\n\n2. Simplify the expression inside the square root:\n   \\[\n   \\sqrt{36} - 3\n   \\]\n\n3. Calculate the square root:\n   \\[\n   6 - 3\n   \\]\n\n4. Subtract 3 from the result:\n   \\[\n   3\n   \\]\n\nTherefore, the value of \\(\\sqrt{x^2} - 3\\) when \\(x = 6\\) is \\(\\boxed{3}\\)."
