"First, we need to determine the speed of the robot in kilometers per hour. Since the robot takes 2.5 hours to travel 1 kilometer, its speed is:\n\n\\[\n\\text{Speed} = \\frac{1 \\text{ km}}{2.5 \\text{ hours}} = 0.4 \\text{ km/h}\n\\]\n\nNext, we need to find the distance the robot travels 90 seconds at this speed. Since 90 seconds is equivalent to \\(\\frac{9}{10}\\) hours, the distance traveled is:\n\n\\[\n\\text{Distance} = 0.4 \\text{ km/h} \\times \\frac{9}{10} \\text{ hours} = 0.36 \\text{ km}\n\\]\n\nTo convert this distance from kilometers to meters, we multiply by 1000:\n\n\\[\n\\text{Distance in meters} = 0.36 \\text{ km} \\times 1000 \\text{ meters/km} = 360 \\text{ meters}\n\\]\n\nTherefore, the length of the hallway is \\(\\boxed{360}\\) meters."
