"The intersection of plane $P$ and line $L$ is the point that lies on both $P$ and $L$. We can find this point by solving the system of equations given by the parameterizations of $P$ and $L$.\n\nThe equation of plane $P$ is\n\\[2x - y - z = 0.\\]\nThe equation of line $L$ is\n\\[x = 7 + 3u,\\]\n\\[y = 4,\\]\n\\[z = 1 - u.\\]\n\nSubstituting the equations of line $L$ into the equation of plane $P$, we get\n\\[2(7 + 3u) - 4 - (1 - u) = 0.\\]\nSimplifying, we get\n\\[14 + 6u - 4 - 1 + u = 0,\\]\n\\[7 + 7u = 0,\\]\n\\[u = -\\frac{7}{7}.\\]\n\nTherefore, the intersection of plane $P$ and line $L$ is $\\boxed{0}$."
